---
system: sys-09-ota-release-management
flow_id: device-check-and-download
surface: device
spec_anchor: /software/systems/09-ota-release-management#ota-check-flow-device-facing
actors: [Device, Gateway, OtaService, S3, CloudFront, PostgreSQL]
apis:
  - GET /v1/ota/check
  - POST /v1/ota/result
externals: [S3, CloudFront]
queues: []
failure_paths:
  - rate_limited_4_per_24h
  - stuck_device_3_failures
  - cohort_excluded
  - rollout_not_eligible
  - manifest_signature_invalid
  - binary_sha_mismatch
  - signed_url_expired
idempotency: ota_attempts rows append-only per (device_id, firmware_release_id, status); device deduplicates by checking current version before download
retry: device retries at next 6h interval if signed URL expired; auto-skipped after 3 failures in 7 days
timeout: 10s check · 120s download p95
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Device
    participant Gateway
    participant OtaService
    participant S3
    participant CloudFront
    participant PostgreSQL

    Device->>Gateway: GET /v1/ota/check (mTLS) {X-Device-Id, X-Firmware-Version, X-Hardware-Revision, X-Battery-Percent, X-RSSI}
    Gateway->>OtaService: forward
    OtaService->>PostgreSQL: validate device exists
    alt rate_limited_4_per_24h
        OtaService-->>Device: 429 rate_limited (ota_check_rate_limited_total inc)
    else stuck_device_3_failures
        OtaService->>PostgreSQL: COUNT ota_attempts WHERE status IN ('failed','rollback') AND completed_at > now() - 7d
        PostgreSQL-->>OtaService: >=3
        OtaService-->>Device: 304 no_update (auto-skipped)
    else cohort_excluded
        OtaService->>PostgreSQL: cohort filtering check (sys-08 fleet_cohorts)
        OtaService-->>Device: 304 no_update
    else rollout_not_eligible
        OtaService->>OtaService: bucket = SHA-256 of deviceId+releaseId first 4 bytes mod 100, eligible if bucket below rollout_percentage
        OtaService-->>Device: 304 no_update
    else already_on_version
        OtaService-->>Device: 304 no_update
    else success
        OtaService->>CloudFront: generate signed URL (1h expiry) for binary + manifest
        CloudFront-->>OtaService: signed URLs
        OtaService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT ota_attempts {status='offered', from_version, to_version, battery_percent_at_start, rssi_at_start}
        OtaService-->>Device: 200 {manifest_url, signature, min_battery_percent, min_rssi_dbm, binary_sha256, binary_size_bytes}
    end

    Device->>CloudFront: GET signed manifest URL
    CloudFront-->>Device: manifest JSON + signature
    Device->>Device: bootloader verifies ECDSA P-256 signature with factory-embedded public key
    alt manifest_signature_invalid
        Device->>Device: REJECT, retain current FW, emit fault telemetry
    else success
        Device->>Device: anti-downgrade check, min battery+RSSI check
        Device->>CloudFront: GET signed binary URL (status=downloading)
        alt signed_url_expired
            CloudFront--xDevice: 403
            Device->>Device: retry at next ota_check cycle
        else success
            CloudFront-->>Device: gzipped binary
            Device->>Device: decompress, SHA-256, compare to manifest
            alt binary_sha_mismatch
                Device->>Device: REJECT — tampered download
            else success
                Device->>Device: validate ELF header, flash to inactive OTA slot, A/B swap, reboot, verify
            end
        end
    end

    Device->>Gateway: POST /v1/ota/result {release_id, status='success'|'failed'|'rollback', failure_code, download_duration_ms, flash_duration_ms}
    Gateway->>OtaService: forward
    OtaService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE ota_attempts SET status, completed_at, failure_code
    OtaService-->>Device: 204

    Note over Device,PostgreSQL: timeout 10s check / 120s download p95 · signed URL 1h · auto-skip after 3 failures in 7d
